# Changelog

When making user-facing changes to the project (bug fixes, new features, enhancements, breaking changes,
documentation that changes how the template is used), add an entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.

This project is continuously improved and **does not follow semantic versioning or use an `[Unreleased]` section**.
Entries are grouped under a date heading, newest first:

```markdown
## September 9, 2026

- Short description of the change, in the past tense
```

Before adding an entry, read the top of `CHANGELOG.md`. If a heading for today's date already exists, append a
bullet to it rather than creating a second heading for the same date.

Skip changelog entries for refactors, code style changes, or other internal-only changes with no user-facing impact.
